 "notes": "PSP (Parker Solar Probe) in-situ DPDM->photon resonant-conversion search. Headline curve is the blue PSP 95% C.L. envelope in Fig.2 (constraint_eps.pdf), extracted as the vector stroke path of the region lower boundary; tick-calibrated (mass 10^-10..10^-7 eV, y 10^-15..10^-11) and cross-checked against both the mass and top frequency axes. y-axis is epsilon*(rho_A/rho_DM)^0.5; reported value = chi assuming DPDM is 100% of local DM, so chi = plotted value directly (no chi^2, report chi). Paper does not quote a numerical local DM density (density enters via Eq.3 P0 ~ rho_DM but no value stated), hence dm_density_assumed=null. Frequency 70 kHz-20 MHz => m_A ~ 3e-10..8e-8 eV (right end matches 8e-8 exactly; plotted curve extends slightly below 70 kHz to ~1.2e-10 eV on the left). Curve is a jagged per-frequency-bin envelope; ~10^-14 at low mass rising to ~few*10^-13 at high mass, consistent with abstract eps<~10^-14..10^-13. STEREO (orange) and CMB (gray) regions are comparisons, not this measurement.",
